{"title":"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Existence\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Existence</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Minimality\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Minimality</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a set with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed2fa2a4d1f8c024da24d87119ecb00f4a36888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A| = 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has 225 elements.  Suppose further that there are eleven subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/6/e26b63cf52b85e36ddb448caf62ff9fc413bce8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca79d8deb15b4682a49e4040736c18f2725390f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A_i | = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3e52219c2c651752cdf56cca7f8a20073386e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e802ff1811f123978cf75af969c2af42ded07c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A_i \\cap A_j| = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad19b6e98d4264bb67d4dffd7732789e7c0289c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i &lt; j \\le 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa7684225ea083fac9c9ae39a49e8eab2f31552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A_1 \\cup A_2 \\cup \\dots \\cup A_{11}| \\ge 165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />, and give an example for which equality holds.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Existence\">Existence</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Existence\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/958bcce28272a8d2cb1eec88135d8b8180bb9f6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle \\binom{11}3 = 165,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"85\" height=\"22\" /> and so it is natural to consider placing one element in each intersection of three of the 11 sets. Since each pair of sets is in 9 3-way intersections&#8212;one with each of the 9 remaining sets&#8212;any two sets will have 9 elements in common. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed7072051f5bcdf2a7b6673b4503d33997d3591.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle \\binom{10}2 = 45,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"76\" height=\"22\" /> each set is in 45 triples and thus will have 45 elements. We can now throw in 60 more elements outside the union of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and we are done.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Minimality\">Minimality</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Minimality\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>As in the proof of PIE, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be a finite set. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ace0adcf302814c363e25c00b1696bd6200a56a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle U = \\bigcup_{i\\in I} A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"95\" height=\"19\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c991561f447049959d3d046bec53538edfefa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\in I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5322621e2d50ee17566bcf467769fc0d47710a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\chi_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> be the <i>characteristic function</i> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, that is, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/1/b012cd70c9820fa803ebdc4ae27e030ae9165b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha \\in U,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6e2a9850f9103864d442ab2b6be7f3234ab158.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\chi_i(\\alpha) = \\begin{cases} 1 &amp; \\alpha \\in A_i \\\\ 0 &amp; \\alpha \\not\\in A_i \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3eef8699e4379af6fff4e2efe3704f4a6c640f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha \\in U$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb44286ba400b440705b19a53675203e4cabe74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle n_\\alpha = \\sum_{i \\in I} \\chi_i(\\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"129\" height=\"19\" />, that is the number of subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> of which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is an element.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e07d4ea59d93a0d2bb67843af9ccdc1114513f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\subset I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3d6fc121e0a419135c21267b5f58a78998758df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle A_S = \\bigcap_{i \\in S}A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"106\" height=\"19\" />. Then the characteristic function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/7247ed9d644429d8de4fa3b5038b3b5ea91dc545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce49ea5de7fb6cb01a75ba8ce53267f2d425724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle \\prod_{i \\in S} \\chi_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />.\nThe number of elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/7247ed9d644429d8de4fa3b5038b3b5ea91dc545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> is simply the sum of its characteristic function over all the elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb106b953d36e74735237734852307531ae6b168.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|A_S| = \\sum_{\\alpha \\in U} \\prod_{i \\in S} \\chi_i(\\alpha).\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"39\" />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3de5c7044dd91c2fdb440ccea140b7083b3b7656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le k \\le |I|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />, consider the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/35571445c421c5a951a0bdff91643a9c6ea1ecda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b76bd02531e299901a9b54e62b2f7967b2641a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A_S|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> over all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc2eaed3eab064d0f37707b1a87ae80b565b668a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S\\subset I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/59620e0116df6b35de8f454ede6e1249fe697aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S|= k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. This is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85af292252fd90dc57fa163c96d535c800133fc8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N_k = \\sum_{\\substack{S\\subset I\\\\|S| = k}} \\sum_{\\alpha \\in U} \\prod_{i \\in S} \\chi_i(\\alpha) = \\sum_{\\substack{S\\subset I\\\\|S| = k}} |A_S|\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"52\" />\nreversing the order summation, as an element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> that appears in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8eb27d8f3d3e5ea2bb7159d68915b259934467cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"10\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, will appear in exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f1ace461b25c98932bf6dc22b8627228f07a1a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle \\binom{n_\\alpha}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"30\" height=\"22\" /> intersections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> subsets, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a75d93b20ee59fad2ed97ce59a95c336e32ddb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{\\substack{S\\subset I\\\\|S| = k}} |A_S| = \\sum_{\\alpha \\in U} \\sum_{\\substack{S\\subset I\\\\|S| = k}} \\prod_{i \\in S} \\chi_i(\\alpha) = \\sum_{\\alpha \\in U} \\binom{n_\\alpha}k.\\]\" width=\"337\" height=\"66\" />\n</p><p>Applying the above with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a7f393ba1027dea5e0fc352f2537a667e10d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I = \\{1, 2, \\ldots, 11\\},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, since each of the 11 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> has 45 elements, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e4c487599e6e3ee64171b5de832fc55ee056a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N_1 = \\sum_{\\alpha \\in U} n_\\alpha = 11 \\cdot 45,\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"38\" />\nand for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e44ca2cae6be42148fe1b1fd8b5d55bd6b599bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, since each of the 55 pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/1/5c1127962673db0eadf005686a16c39f94cdc18e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i \\cap A_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" /> has 9 elements, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b82782a2fb9aa38cb813554f988dabcb4ccdbf42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N_2 = \\sum_{\\alpha \\in U} \\binom{n_\\alpha}2 = 9 \\cdot 55 = 11 \\cdot 45.\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Therefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b553de72f9ef5eed30f40738dca47d28346849e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} s_1 &amp;= \\sum_{\\alpha \\in U} n_\\alpha = N_1 = 11\\cdot45 \\\\ s_2 &amp;= \\sum_{\\alpha \\in U} n_\\alpha^2 = 2N_2 + N_1 = 3\\cdot11\\cdot45. \\end{align*}\" width=\"290\" height=\"87\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e1a3440873e7a2f3fe506874511258f4ec57533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = |U|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> be the number of elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />.\nSince for any set of real numbers the mean value of the squares is greater than or equal to the square of the mean value, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/8048196dbe4904096afa64949f8eec83a345dfa7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{s_2}n \\ge \\left(\\frac{s_1}n\\right)^2 \\implies n \\ge \\frac{s_1^2}{s_2} = \\frac{11^2\\cdot 45^2}{3\\cdot11\\cdot45} = \\frac{11\\cdot45}3 = 165.\\]\" width=\"428\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78f6d149ca40477869f14a3d92e661be7f063197.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|U| \\ge 165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> as required.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will count the number of ordered triples, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e2a4e317953d51e15db09549003a6d02260334d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A_i,A_j,x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e7742c1ce0b37c0e74d3b7216e01a03a34f6baef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i,j\\le11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1898c544355d72dcd10aab8eaeb78c02136a2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in A_i \\cap A_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" />. We know this is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5e1d3bd9441335b7b1aba0e97a537119b61b75a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$990=11\\cdot10\\cdot9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"14\" />­. We can also find that this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba119903846eca3100329d3b25daa83c8d0d1c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{225}b_k^2-b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"82\" height=\"50\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is the number of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> subsets the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb9fb3b35f43cc27e4e63da0093b956154335a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is in. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/1/e71ee8c3d1807e575c19c4df45a67bf8e54c8bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{225}b_k=45\\cdot11=495$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"169\" height=\"50\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e40ad8b2cfa0b5743f0f480db5e7887b3c9e8e01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{225}b_k^2=990+495=1485$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"205\" height=\"50\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95b2b28f2f011b37b01566bfd6ae72b598ebf512.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=|A_1 \\cup A_2 \\cup \\dots \\cup A_{11}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c2c6068ad14e22881b57e87e829d1493a2ccbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8eb0f11cc3d005e5044d8c8710e101d0526eb3a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le k\\le225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. By the QM-AM inequality, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79cdb5b5de1a50f1e3247351879e96169ee4bad8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sum_{k=1}^{225}b_k^2}n\\ge\\Bigg(\\frac{\\sum_{k=1}^{225}b_k}n\\Bigg)^2\\implies\\frac{1485}n\\ge\\Big(\\frac{495}n\\Big)^2\\implies n\\ge165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"478\" height=\"57\" /> and that equality occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/4/e74362d60cb27d146672e9b06e524f9beb338a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1=b_2=b_3=\\cdots=b_{165}=3,b_{166}=b_{167}=\\cdots=b_{225}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"446\" height=\"16\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Solution by randomdude10807\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> to be the amount of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> such that the element is contained exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> times among the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6edb286660f22d694ff4152ede3c948864cbb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />. We are trying to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/a/a5aa3c72cb2f7db6c2c584a5985d3184334aa534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{11}x_i\\ge 165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"98\" height=\"55\" />. Now, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d7584d8f9f1b57665d1e6666dd9d7ae4449caa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{11}ix_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"53\" height=\"55\" /> is equivalent to the total amount of not necessarily distinct elements among the subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6edb286660f22d694ff4152ede3c948864cbb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/7/28771f722e3278093127f03446d3d03a8bb7693a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{11}ix_i=11|A_j|=495$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"177\" height=\"55\" />. Furthermore, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed4e35146f57ac70688981b430e841aeca38841.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{11}\\binom{i}{2}x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"84\" height=\"55\" /> is equivalent to the total amount of not necessarily distinct pairs of subsets such that the subsets share an element. In other words, each subset pair should be counted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times in this sum, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/2614b7249042a1565dbd265c273d5fe892dfcec3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{11}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"42\" height=\"53\" /> total distinct pairs of subsets, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/7/b87b97520dece6d9c8f3e6dbace86017113f352a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{11}\\binom{i}{2}x_i=9*\\binom{11}{2}=495$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"232\" height=\"55\" />. Noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/b/73b9c0a4e033b558ab51418b81afe092348f7b0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\binom{i}{2}+i=i^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"115\" height=\"55\" /> for all nonnegative integers, we note\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe8fe20839b7a26aeeed9ac487626308cef01c67.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{11}i^2x_i=2(\\sum_{i=1}^{11}\\binom{i}{2}x_i)+(\\sum_{i=1}^{11}ix_i)=495*2+495=495*3\\]\" width=\"479\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Finally, CS inequality gives us\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64fd52743e8c5a6ae3d7277a9664747f2c41714e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\sum_{i=1}^{11}i^2x_i)(\\sum_{i=1}^{11}x_i)\\ge(\\sum_{i=1}^{11}ix_i)^2\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"50\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd635617e97f59d9615501b96cb9d4968cfc4524.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(495*3)(\\sum_{i=1}^{11}x_i)\\ge(495^2)\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"50\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6d042816b75ff64bba6db1a9cd22a30b0f7ee23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{(\\sum_{i=1}^{11}x_i)\\ge 165}\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"65\" />\nas desired. \n</p><p>One equality case occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b69357b90db9b0ec6892cd2e6fb5bbbc10adeab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbdc2da85bbcf4646678b96bec1cbf21c0379646.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3=165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" />. Choose any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249f6c7d94f60f07968395ca19214325629974d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$165$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> elements, and represent each with a unique combination of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> subsets (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa1ae6ef2b0ab64619f224efba51d8ce011999e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{11}{3}=165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"97\" height=\"53\" />). It is then obvious that each subset has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> distinct elements, because after each subset is chosen, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc61bcd70dd08ca88b8f214b03d595ad1613d97a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{10}{2}=45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"88\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose the other two subsets to produce a unique element. Similarly, each pair of subsets shares exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> elements, because after choosing the two subsets, we can choose one of the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> subsets to produce the unique element. Hence, proved. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd55f34d0154b833e4c1570c01cf915587839d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~SigmaPiE\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\">USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO\" title=\"2011 USAMO\">2011 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\"><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017225328\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.054 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.075 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 586/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1261/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 54/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20078/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.202      1 -total\n 49.68%    7.055      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 49.01%    6.960      